            "subject": "LU-20663 rustreapi: write the stripe pattern through the union"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Robert Read",
          "email": "rread@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-08-29 00:06:59.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Robert Read",
          "email": "rread@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-08-31 15:10:31.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20664 rustreapi: NUL-terminate the pool name",
        "message": "LU-20664 rustreapi: NUL-terminate the pool name\n\nOpenOptions::get_stripe_param() pointed lsp_pool at the bytes of a\nRust String, which carries no trailing NUL.  liblustreapi reads that\nfield as a C string -- lov_pool_is_ignored(), the strlen() in\nllapi_stripe_param_verify(), and the \"%s\" into lum_pool_name -- so\neach read runs past the end of the String's allocation until it finds\na zero byte.  A valid pool then fails with EINVAL or ENOENT, trips\nthe LOV_MAXPOOLNAME check, or faults.\n\nThe memory itself is fine: self.pool outlives the call.  Only the\nterminator is missing, so copy into a CString.  Return it rather than\ndropping it at the end of get_stripe_param(), since the caller uses\nparam after the call returns; both callers hold it in a named binding\nfor the duration.\n\nAn interior NUL cannot be a pool name, so report it instead of\nsilently truncating.\n\nTested with cargo test -p rustreapi --lib stripe_param_pool.\n\nSigned-off-by: Robert Read <rread@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I00c4376ca7dac139622e060b6d3f8d59d2fdf31d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
